1
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:24,000
They weren't born in the wild... They were shipped there.

2
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Madagascar is a family, animation, adventure film directed by Eric Darnell.

3
00:12:54,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Four animal friends get a taste of the wild life when they break out of captivity at
the Central Park Zoo and wash ashore on the island of Madagascar.

4
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Alex (voice), played by Ben Stiller.

5
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Marty (voice), played by Chris Rock.

6
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:54,000
Melman (voice), played by David Schwimmer.

7
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:12,000
Gloria (voice), played by Jada Pinkett Smith.

8
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Julien (voice), played by Sacha Baron Cohen.

9
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:48,000
Maurice (voice), played by Cedric the Entertainer.

10
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
Madagascar is a 2005 American animated survival comedy film directed by Eric Darnell and
Tom McGrath, and written by Mark Burton, Billy Frolick, Darnell and McGrath.

11
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:24,000
Produced by DreamWorks Animation and PDI/DreamWorks, the film stars the voices of Ben Stiller, Chris Rock, David Schwimmer and Jada Pinkett Smith as a quartet of
anthropomorphic animals from the Central Park Zoo who find themselves stranded on the island of Madagascar and must adjust to living in the wild.

12
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:42,000
The film features a musical score by Hans Zimmer.

13
00:55:54,000 --> 00:56:00,000
It also features a cover version of "I Like to Move It" by Sacha Baron Cohen, which
has since become a recurring theme song throughout the franchise.

14
01:00:12,000 --> 01:00:18,000
Madagascar was released in the United States by
DreamWorks Pictures on May 27, 2005.

15
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics, who praised the
visuals and charm but criticized the story and humor.

16
01:08:48,000 --> 01:08:54,000
It was a success at the box office, grossing $558 million on a production budget
of $75 million, becoming the sixth highest-grossing film of 2005.

17
01:13:06,000 --> 01:13:12,000
The success of Madagascar launched a multimedia franchise, which includes two sequels, a spin-off film, several short
films, television series and specials and a number of video games, theme park attractions and live stage shows.

18
01:17:24,000 --> 01:17:30,000
The film explores themes of friendship, island, escape, africa, lion.

19
01:21:42,000 --> 01:21:48,000
The tone is lighthearted.
